        "id": "Johnny-kgc",
        "title": "Johnny — Google Meet AI Meeting Bot",
        "type": "epic",
        "description": "Johnny is a single-user AI assistant that joins Google Meet meetings on the user's behalf and can listen, transcribe, suggest replies, ask for approval, or speak autonomously within configured constraints.\n\nRuns as a daemon stack (Docker Compose) with a SvelteKit web UI for calendar browsing, per-meeting configuration, and real-time approval/transcript visibility.\n\nBuilt around three swappable layers:\n1. Meeting connector — Playwright+Chromium driving a real Google Meet session\n2. Voice-agent pipeline — Pipecat with LiveKit transport adapter\n3. Provider-agnostic STT/LLM/TTS adapters — cloud and local from day one\n\nAll meeting data (transcripts, router decisions, agent utterances) persisted to PostgreSQL with pgvector for transcript search.\n\n## Goals\n- Mark calendar events for Johnny to attend, with per-meeting context and behavior mode\n- Four bot modes: listen-only, suggest-only, approval-required, limited auto-speak\n- Provider adapters from day one (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, Deepgram, ElevenLabs, faster-whisper, vLLM/Ollama, Piper)\n- Local Docker Compose with PostgreSQL, Redis, FastAPI, SvelteKit, isolated meet-worker containers per active meeting\n- Join as dedicated bot Google account or user's own account, configurable per meeting\n- Persist full meeting audit log for post-meeting review",
        "metadata": {
          "dependencyCount": 0,
          "dependentCount": 0
        }
      }
    ],
